IMPORT `pet-bill`

-- FICTIONAL: the LQA checker's worked example.

`Rex, minded by a neighbour` MEANS Situation WITH
    `age in calendar months`            IS 6
    `days the owner has kept the pet`   IS 400
    `days the minder has kept the pet`  IS 5
    `the pet is registered`             IS FALSE

-- R-01: the readings of "the person" part company. On reading A the duty applies;
-- on reading B it does not.
#ASSERT `the owner must ensure the pet is registered` `Rex, minded by a neighbour`
#ASSERT `section 3(2) disapplies the duty, reading B` `Rex, minded by a neighbour`

`Pip, at three months` MEANS Situation WITH
    `age in calendar months`            IS 3
    `days the owner has kept the pet`   IS 90
    `days the minder has kept the pet`  IS 90
    `the pet is registered`             IS FALSE

-- T-04: the duty attaches at three complete calendar months.
#ASSERT `the owner must ensure the pet is registered` `Pip, at three months`
